// Title: Suspicious Binary Writes Via AnyDesk
// Sigma ID: 2d367498-5112-4ae5-a06a-96e7bc33a211
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-09-28 | Modified: 2025-02-24
// ATT&CK: command-and-control, T1219.002
// Description: Detects AnyDesk writing binary files to disk other than "gcapi.dll". According to RedCanary
//   research it is highly abnormal for AnyDesk to write executable files to disk besides gcapi.dll,
//   which is a legitimate DLL that is part of the Google Chrome web browser used to interact with
//   the Google Cloud API. (See reference section for more details)
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://redcanary.com/blog/misbehaving-rats/
//   - https://thedfirreport.com/2025/02/24/confluence-exploit-leads-to-lockbit-ransomware/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/file/file_event/file_event_win_anydesk_writing_susp_binaries.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where ((InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\AnyDesk.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\AnyDeskMSI.exe") and (FolderPath endswith ".dll" or FolderPath endswith ".exe")) and (not(FolderPath endswith "\\gcapi.dll"))
